Guided Exercise: Automatic Image Updates with OpenShift Image Change Triggers
Objective
Automatically update an application deployment using OpenShift image streams and image change triggers, then roll back if needed.
________________________________________
1. Prepare the Lab Environment
lab start updates-triggers
•	Sets up project updates-triggers.
•	Deploys a web application (version deployment) with 10 replicas.
•	Prepares curl_loop.sh to test live updates.
Login and set project:
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
oc project updates-triggers
________________________________________
2. Inspect Image Stream
Check local lookup policy and existing tags:
oc set image-lookup
# Output should show: versioned-hello  true
oc get istag
oc get istag versioned-hello:1 -o jsonpath='{.tag.from.name}{"\n"}'
•	Confirms versioned-hello:1 exists.
•	Shows SHA ID of source image.
________________________________________
3. Inspect Deployment
oc get deployment -o wide
•	Deployment: version
•	Container: versioned-hello
•	Image: versioned-hello:1 (resolved to SHA ID)
________________________________________
4. Run Continuous Test Requests
/home/student/DO180/labs/updates-triggers/curl_loop.sh
•	Sends repeated requests to the deployed application.
•	Leave running to observe rolling updates.
________________________________________
5. Add Image Trigger to Deployment
oc set triggers deployment/version \
  --from-image versioned-hello:1 --containers versioned-hello
Verify trigger:
oc get deployment version \
  -o jsonpath='{.metadata.annotations.image\.openshift\.io/triggers}' | jq .
•	Confirms Deployment watches versioned-hello:1.
________________________________________
6. Update Image Stream Tag
oc tag registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/versioned-hello:1-125 versioned-hello:1
•	Triggers rolling update.
•	Observe in curl_loop.sh:
o	Old pods respond initially.
o	During rollout, both old and new pods respond.
o	After rollout, only new version (v1.1) responds.
Verify deployment now uses new SHA:
oc get deployment version -o wide
oc describe is versioned-hello
________________________________________
7. Roll Back Deployment
Revert the image stream tag to previous SHA:
oc tag registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/versioned-hello@sha256:66e0...105e versioned-hello:1
•	Triggers rollback.
•	Observe curl_loop.sh:
o	Pods with old version (v1.0) respond again.
________________________________________
8. Finish Lab
lab finish updates-triggers
•	Cleans up resources to avoid affecting future exercises.
________________________________________
Key Concepts
1.	Image triggers automatically roll out deployments when an image stream tag changes.
2.	SHA IDs ensure reproducible deployments.
3.	Rolling updates: old and new pods coexist during rollout.
4.	Rollback is simple by reverting the tag to the previous SHA.
5.	Useful for managing updates safely in production-like environment

